.TH CHTTP_PATCH 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttp_patch \- do a PATCH request with the default client
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpclient.h>

ccol_retval_t chttp_patch(const char *url,
                          const chttp_request_body_t *body,
                          chttpcli_response **resp_out);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This is a convenience wrapper that sends an HTTP PATCH.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
The same codes as chttpclient_do, plus ccol_invalid_args for a body
whose data is NULL while its len is not zero, which
chttp_request_create refuses. ccol_not_enough_memory also covers a
failed allocation of the internal request object.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttp_get (3),
.BR chttp_do (3)
